# Reuse first: search before you build

## Pyramid Layer

- Layer: L0 gate. Runs before new code exists.

## Use This When

- A task implies a new function, type, constant, component, Zod schema, port or adapter.

## Stop Here If

- You found an existing artifact to reuse or extend, or you searched and can name where the new one belongs and why nothing fits.

## Descend To

- UI: `packages/ui/src/components/` and `packages/ui/src/components/platform/`.
- Identifiers: `packages/ids` (entity-id registry); never mint ids another way.
- Domain building blocks: `packages/kernel` (entities, value objects, events, exceptions, specifications, text sorting).
- Dependency wiring: `packages/di`; message buses: `packages/cqrs`.
- Oversized files worth splitting before extending: `bun run refactor:scan`.

## Core rule

- Search the workspace (file names and symbols) before writing a helper, util, type or config reader. A second implementation of something that exists is a defect, not a style choice.
- Extend the existing artifact when it is the same concept; create a new one only for a genuinely different concept, in the package that owns that concept.
